@startuml
title SE104 Survey System - Survey State Diagram

skinparam shadowing false

[*] --> Draft : Create survey\nSave as draft
[*] --> Published : Create survey\nPublish immediately

state Draft {
  [*] --> Editable
  Editable : Owner can view in dashboard
  Editable : Owner can manage or delete
  Editable : Public link is not answerable
}

state Published {
  [*] --> Active
  Active : Public survey page is answerable
  Active : Views and submissions are collected
  Active : Analytics and exports are available to owner
  Active --> Unrestricted : No allowed respondent emails
  Active --> Restricted : Allowed respondent emails exist
  Unrestricted : Anyone with the link can respond
  Restricted : Matching signed-in email required
  Restricted : Wrong signed-in account can change account
}

state Archived {
  [*] --> Retained
  Retained : Public survey page is not answerable
  Retained : Owner can retain management and analytics access
}

Draft --> Published : Owner publishes draft
Published --> Archived : Owner archives published survey

Draft --> Deleted : Owner confirms delete
Published --> Deleted : Owner confirms delete
Archived --> Deleted : Owner confirms delete

Deleted --> [*]

note right of Archived
Current UI does not support
republishing archived surveys.
end note

note bottom of Draft
Sharing a link or QR code
does not change survey state.
end note

note right of Published
Access list changes do not
change the survey lifecycle state;
they only affect who may open
and submit the published survey.
end note

@enduml
